msgid "Photolith API"
msgstr ""

msgid "Conventions"
msgstr ""

msgid "All endpoints live under ``/api/v1/``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Authenticate with a per-user API token, issued via the admin interface or"
" ``./manage.py create_api_token <username>``::"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This works for any Photolith URL, including ``/search/data/``. The user's"
" existing permissions apply. An unknown token returns ``401``, rather "
"than redirecting to the login page."
msgstr ""

msgid "Request & response bodies are JSON, except for image upload."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Status codes: ``200`` OK, ``201`` created, ``400`` invalid input, ``401``"
" bad token, ``403`` forbidden, ``404`` not found, ``409`` conflict, "
"``412`` precondition failed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Errors use the same shape as existing JSON views, plus per-field errors "
"when a form fails validation (e.g. annotations):"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Bounding boxes, scale lines & axis polygons are ``[[x, y], ...]`` arrays "
"in image pixel co-ordinates, as stored by the web client."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Individual metadata uses the same type-prefixed keys as the ingest form: "
"``ch_`` (text), ``nm_`` (number), ``in_`` (integer), ``dt_`` (date/time),"
" ``tx_`` (taxonomy, e.g. ``{\"id\": 1}``)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Python client"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``photolith_client/`` in the Photolith repository is a Python package "
"wrapping this API, e.g. for batch-import tools. It depends only on "
"`requests <https://requests.readthedocs.io/>`_, and can be installed "
"without the rest of Photolith::"
msgstr ""

msgid "See ``photolith_client/README.md`` for usage."
msgstr ""

msgid "Who am I"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``GET /api/v1/whoami/``: Check a token & what it can do before starting a"
" batch:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Images"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``POST /api/v1/images/``: Upload an image (requires ``add_image``), the "
"request body is the raw file::"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Images are stored by content hash, so uploading the same file twice "
"returns the existing image (``200`` rather than ``201``, ``created`` is "
"false):"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``GET /api/v1/images/<id>/``: Fetch an image object (requires "
"``view_image``), as above without ``created``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``PATCH /api/v1/images/<id>/``: Set the image's scale. Requires "
"``add_individual``, as when setting the scale whilst ingesting. Keys not "
"given are left alone, ``null`` clears:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Individuals on an image"
msgstr ""

msgid "``GET /api/v1/images/<id>/individuals/``: All individuals on an image:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The response includes an ``ETag`` header."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``PUT /api/v1/images/<id>/individuals/``: Replace the full set of "
"individuals on an image. Every existing individual must be included by "
"``id``, either to update it, or with a ``null`` bounding box to delete "
"it. Entries without an ``id`` create new individuals:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A newly uploaded image has no individuals, so can be PUT to straight "
"away. Otherwise (e.g. the upload returned ``\"created\": false``, as the "
"image already existed), GET the image's individuals first, and match them"
" to your own records (e.g. by ``ch_slideLabel`` & ``ch_individualLabel``)"
" to find their IDs. Leaving any out returns ``400``, rather than deleting"
" them."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Within an image, individuals are identified to people by the combination "
"of ``ch_slideLabel`` & ``ch_individualLabel``, e.g. individual ``3`` can "
"be on more than one slide. So every entry not being deleted must have "
"both labels, and the combination cannot repeat within the request. Labels"
" can be changed, as the ``id`` identifies the individual."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Each entry's ``data`` replaces that individual's metadata, keys not given"
" are removed."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The update is all-or-nothing: if any entry is invalid, nothing is saved. "
"Errors, and the rest of the response, refer to entries by their position "
"in the request, e.g. ``\"fields\": {\"individuals[1].data.tx_species\": "
"[...]}``. Existing individuals missing from the request are reported in "
"``\"fields\": {\"individuals\": [...]}``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The API never deletes annotations as a side-effect. If the update would "
"change the bounding box of, or remove, an individual with annotations, "
"nothing is saved and ``409`` is returned, listing annotation IDs by "
"entry. The client is responsible for deleting these annotations first "
"(see below), and if it cannot, it should not be changing those "
"individuals:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Send the ``ETag`` from a previous GET as ``If-Match`` to get ``412`` "
"instead of overwriting changes made since."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On success, the response is the same as GET, plus the individual IDs "
"changed by each entry, including those created:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``PATCH /api/v1/individuals/<id>/``: Update a single individual, ``<id>``"
" is the individual's ID from the GET / PUT responses above. ``data`` is "
"merged with existing metadata:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Changing the bounding box of an individual with annotations returns "
"``409``, as above, but ``annotations`` is a list of IDs, e.g. ``[9001]``."
" Changing the labels to those of another individual on the image returns "
"``400``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``DELETE /api/v1/individuals/<id>/``: Delete an individual. Returns "
"``409``, as PATCH, if it has annotations."
msgstr ""

msgid "Finding individuals"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use the existing ``/search/data/`` endpoint, which accepts API tokens. "
"Filters are the same as the search form, e.g::"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``nm_`` / ``in_`` / ``dt_`` filters are ranges, so give the same value "
"twice for an exact match. Add ``with_associated_images=1`` to include "
"``image_id`` in each row. Metadata is flattened into each row, rather "
"than nested under ``data``:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With ``with_annotations``, each row also includes ``annotation_id`` (for "
"e.g. ``DELETE /api/v1/annotations/<id>/``) and ``project_id`` (``null`` "
"for annotations not in a project), both ``null`` for individuals without "
"annotations. ``rating`` is returned as stored (``100``/``50``/``0`` for "
"``\"1\"``/``\"2\"``/``\"3\"``)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``num_annotations`` only counts annotations in the ``project`` searched, "
"or without one, annotations not in any project. Use ``num_annotations`` "
"from ``GET /api/v1/images/<id>/individuals/`` for the total, e.g. before "
"a PUT."
msgstr ""

msgid "Clients should check the response for:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``alert``: More than ``SEARCH_RESULT_MAX_ROWS`` results, the list is "
"truncated."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``error_class`` / ``error``: An error occurred part-way through. The "
"status code will still be ``200``."
msgstr ""

msgid "Annotations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``POST /api/v1/individuals/<id>/annotations/``: Add an annotation, "
"``<id>`` is the individual's ID from the GET / PUT responses above:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Returns ``201``:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Validation is as per the annotate form: ``authority`` cannot exceed the "
"user's own level, and ``project`` must be open. Use ``authority: 20`` "
"(\"Automated reader\") for machine-generated readings."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``rating`` uses the official notation: ``\"1\"`` (good), ``\"2\"`` "
"(difficult) or ``\"3\"`` (unreadable)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``DELETE /api/v1/annotations/<id>/``: Delete an annotation. Only the "
"owner (or a superuser) can do this."
msgstr ""

